{"stamp": "1791724109228735505-1349469", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Equivalence.lean", "line_start": 11, "line_end": 24, "replacement": "/-!\n# Localization functors are preserved through equivalences\n\nIn `Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Predicate.lean`, the lemma\n`Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalence_target` already showed that the predicate of localized\ncategories is unchanged when we replace the target category (i.e. the candidate localized category)\nby an equivalent category.\nIn this file, we show the same for the source category\n(`Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalence_source`).\nMore generally, `Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalences` shows that we may replace both the\nsource and target categories by equivalent categories. This is obtained using\n`Localization.isEquivalence` which provide a sufficient condition in order to show\nthat a functor between localized categories is an equivalence.\n-/"}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
{"stamp": "1791724120295818681-1349675", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Preserves/Limits.lean", "line_start": 10, "line_end": 20, "replacement": "/-!\n# Isomorphisms about functors which preserve (co)limits\n\nIf `G` preserves limits, and `C` and `D` have limits, then for any diagram `F : J ⥤ C` we have a\ncanonical isomorphism `preservesLimitIso : G.obj (limit F) ≅ limit (F ⋙ G)`.\nWe also show that we can commute `IsLimit.lift` of a preserved limit with `Functor.mapCone`:\n`(isLimitOfPreserves G t).lift (G.mapCone c₂) = G.map (t.lift c₂)` (`preserves_lift_mapCone`).\n\nThe duals of these are also given. For functors which preserve (co)limits of specific shapes, see\nthe files in the directory `Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Preserves/Shapes/`.\n-/"}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
{"stamp": "1791724125787773908-1349836", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Preserves/Over.lean", "line_start": 10, "line_end": 17, "replacement": "/-!\n\n# Forgetful functor from `Over X` preserves cofiltered limits\n\nNote that `Over.forget X : Over X ⥤ C` already creates all colimits, see\n`Over.createsColimitsOfSize` in `Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Over.lean`.\n-/"}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
{"stamp": "1791724130774312094-1350025", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/HasLimits.lean", "line_start": 702, "line_end": 710, "replacement": "/-- We have lots of lemmas describing how to simplify `colimit.ι F j ≫ _`,\nand combined with `colimit.ext` we rely on these lemmas for many calculations.\n\nHowever, since `Category.assoc` is a `@[simp]` lemma, often expressions are\nright associated, and it's hard to apply these lemmas about `colimit.ι`.\n\nWe thus use `reassoc` to define additional `@[simp]` lemmas, with an arbitrary extra morphism\n(see `Mathlib/Tactic/CategoryTheory/Reassoc.lean`). -/"}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
{"stamp": "1791724138407872165-1350248", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/HasLimits.lean", "line_start": 702, "line_end": 714, "replacement": "/-!\nWe have lots of lemmas describing how to simplify `colimit.ι F j ≫ _`,\nand combined with `colimit.ext` we rely on these lemmas for many calculations.\n\nHowever, since `Category.assoc` is a `@[simp]` lemma, often expressions are\nright associated, and it's hard to apply these lemmas about `colimit.ι`.\n\nWe thus use `reassoc` to define additional `@[simp]` lemmas, with an arbitrary extra morphism\n(see `Mathlib/Tactic/CategoryTheory/Reassoc.lean`).\n-/\n\n/-- The coprojection `colimit.ι F j` followed by `colimit.desc F c` is `c.ι.app j`. -/\n@[reassoc (attr := simp)]\ntheorem colimit.ι_desc {F : J ⥤ C} [HasColimit F] (c : Cocone F) (j : J) :\n    colimit.ι F j ≫ colimit.desc F c = c.ι.app j :=\n  IsColimit.fac _ c j"}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
